<title>INDIA: India HPCL 1996/97 net seen up 19.66 pct.</title>
<headline>India HPCL 1996/97 net seen up 19.66 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net profit of state-run refiner Hindustan Petroleum Corporation Ltd (HPCL) is forecast to rise 19.66 percent to 6.15 billion rupees in the year ended March 31, 1997, according to a consensus of 28 leading securities and brokerage firms polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>The projections ranged from 5.91 billion rupees to 6.79</p>
<p>billion rupees against 5.14 billion rupees a year ago.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>HPCL   ----PAT seen up 19.66%, sales 10.41%</p>
<p>		     Net profit   1995/96    Net sales   1995/96</p>
<p>				(in million rupees)</p>
<p>Average		6,153.33  5,142.40   131,017.21  118,862.80</p>
<p>High		   6,789.00		 162,664.00</p>
<p>Low		    5,910.00		 115,167.00</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
